{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so all parameter priors (`rho`, `alpha`, `sigma`, and `eta`) occur before those parameters are used to construct the latent Gaussian-process function `f`. This preserves the same posterior density because Stan sampling statements add commutative log-density terms. The protected observation `y` remains a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with the built-in `normal` distribution. The data file is unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"// Fit the hyperparameters of a latent-variable Gaussian process with an
// exponentiated quadratic kernel and a Gaussian likelihood

data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] real x;
  vector[N] y;
}
transformed data {
  real delta = 1e-9;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> rho;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
  vector[N] eta;
}
model {
  vector[N] f;

  rho ~ inv_gamma(5, 5);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta ~ normal(0, 1);

  {
    matrix[N, N] L_K;
    matrix[N, N] K = gp_exp_quad_cov(x, alpha, rho);

    // diagonal elements
    for (n in 1 : N) {
      K[n, n] = K[n, n] + delta;
    }

    L_K = cholesky_decompose(K);
    f = L_K * eta;
  }

  y ~ normal(f, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":5,"x":[5.456623530998508,5.964900564428904,3.815397906995553,4.586283317228205,6.556130741604509],"y":[4.0,4.0,2.0,4.0,5.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
